  partName: Camshaft
  description: The Camshaft is a medium-sized, elongated component positioned at
    the middle-left-front of the rocket engine, made of a material that provides
    the necessary strength and durability. Its primary function is to operate the
    engine's valves, ensuring that they open and close at the correct times to facilitate
    efficient combustion and power generation. A notable aspect of the Camshaft is
    that its design must balance the need for precise valve timing with the requirement
    for minimal friction and wear, making it a critical component in the engine's
    valve train.
